# 25. Invoice Details

The invoice details page displays:

```text
Invoice information
Customer information
Invoice items
Subtotal
Tax
Total
Current status
Processing information
Error information
```

If an invoice is in a retryable failed state, the page provides a Retry action.

---

# 26. External Government Service

Tubo is expected to submit invoices to:

```http
POST /government-api/invoices
```

The external service can return:

```text
200 → Success
400 → Invalid Invoice
503 → Temporary Failure
Timeout → No response
```

Each response must be handled differently.

---

# 27. External API Response Handling

| Response      | Handling                          |
| ------------- | --------------------------------- |
| 200           | Mark invoice as `SUBMITTED`       |
| 400           | Mark as failed/non-retryable      |
| 503           | Retry                             |
| Timeout       | Retry carefully                   |
| Network Error | Retry carefully                   |
| 429           | Retry using rate limiting/backoff |

A `400 Invalid Invoice` generally should not be automatically retried because retrying the same invalid request will not correct the payload.

---

# 28. Asynchronous Processing

The API should not wait for the government API to finish before responding to the user.

Instead:

```text
Client
  │
  ▼
Tubo API
  │
  ├── Validate
  ├── Store
  │
  ▼
Queue
  │
  ▼
Worker
  │
  ▼
Government API
```

The API can return:

```http
201 Created
```

once the invoice is safely stored and accepted for processing.

The initial status can be:

```text
PENDING
```

---

# 29. Accepting an Invoice vs Submitting an Invoice

These are different events.

### Accepted by Tubo

Means:

> Tubo successfully validated and persisted the invoice.

### Submitted

Means:

> The external government system confirmed successful receipt.

Therefore:

```text
HTTP 201 Created
```

does not necessarily mean:

```text
SUBMITTED
```

It means the invoice has entered the processing pipeline.

---

# 30. Retry Strategy

Temporary errors should be retried using exponential backoff.

Example:

```text
```
